This is one of the most important features of Quiztopia.

The quiz system must support real-time classroom competitions.

## 6.1 Teacher Quiz Builder

Teachers must be able to:

- Create a quiz.
- Enter a quiz title.
- Add a description.
- Select the subject.
- Select the academic term.
- Add questions.
- Select question types.
- Configure answer options.
- Identify correct answers.
- Assign points.
- Set question timers.
- Preview the quiz.
- Save drafts.
- Publish quizzes.

For the initial release, prioritize multiple-choice questions.

Design the data model so other question types can be added later.

## 6.2 Quiz Lobby

When a teacher hosts a quiz:

- Generate a unique quiz PIN or join code.
- Display the quiz title.
- Display participating teams.
- Display team names and shared avatars.
- Show a waiting status.
- Allow the teacher to start the competition.

Teams join using their shared account.

A team should not be allowed to join the same active quiz multiple times.

## 6.3 Live Quiz Interface

The team interface should display:

- Team name
- Shared avatar
- Current question
- Question number
- Total number of questions
- Countdown timer
- Available answers
- Submit Answer button
- Submission status
- Current team score

The captain operates the device while the team discusses the answer.

After the captain submits an answer:

- Lock the answer.
- Display a submitted confirmation.
- Prevent changes.
- Wait for the next question or results.

## 6.4 Real-Time Synchronization

Use a reliable real-time system.

All participating teams must receive the same active question and timer state.

The teacher must be able to:

- Start a quiz.
- Advance to the next question.
- End the quiz.
- Monitor participating teams.
- View submissions.
- Display results.

Do not rely on frontend countdown timers as the source of truth.

The backend must determine the official question start time and deadline.

A late submission must be rejected even if the client interface has not yet updated.

## 6.5 Answer Validation

Implement server-side validation.

For every submission, verify:

1. The team belongs to the classroom or is eligible for the competition.
2. The quiz is active.
3. The question is currently active.
4. The submission is within the allowed time.
5. The team has not already submitted an answer.
6. The selected answer belongs to that question.

Enforce one submission per team per question using database constraints and server-side logic.

## 6.6 Scoring

Create a configurable scoring system.

The system may consider:

- Correctness
- Question points
- Response time, if enabled

Correct answers earn points.

Incorrect answers should not earn correct-answer points.

The teacher must be able to configure whether response speed affects scoring.

Avoid rewarding speed so heavily that teams are discouraged from discussing answers.

The final quiz results must show:

- Team rank
- Team name
- Shared avatar
- Correct answers
- Total score
- Rewards earned

